&lt;&lt;~ set lares=`aim` from=`lar://operator:operator@hearth/browser.canon.requests` to=`lar://canon-wright:agent@hearth/browser.canon.reports` ooda-ha=`5/declare-glyphs` drift-ward=`the focused tests do not exercise a complete proved-face browser boot`>>

Canon-Wright: Lares (Tasked Spirit): ->✶ ->⏿ ->◇ ->▶ The browser now stands the daemon canon for the proved worn face, passes its document URL in the grants, and names its bag in the daemon VM recipe.

The change uses ''`assembly.catalogHandle`'' because the browser writes the worn face’s catalog rows through that handle. The changed files carry the implementation and focused checks:

* [[face-daemon-canon.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-browser/wt/packages/lararium-browser/src/face-daemon-canon.ts]] — creates or reopens the catalog-named canon document.
* [[open-browser-vessel.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-browser/wt/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts]] — derives the relation after proof and passes the canon grant.
* [[open-browser-daemon-vm.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-browser/wt/packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-daemon-vm.ts]] — adds the face canon bag to the recipe when the relation and grant stand.
* [[face-daemon-canon.test.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-browser/wt/packages/lararium-browser/tests/face-daemon-canon.test.ts]] — checks the granted canon, floor control, and reopening.

Validation:

* Browser build and stamp, browser typecheck, and `evergreen-boundary` passed.
* Focused browser tests: ''3 passed''.
* Node daemon canon mirror tests: ''6 passed'', using a temporary source-alias runner configuration. The normal runner stopped at its missing node-build guard; building node would have written under the restricted package.
* Full browser suite: ''511 passed, 18 failed, 1 expected failure, 10 skipped'', across 96 files; two of the 12 failed files could not be imported. An isolated rerun confirmed ''5 `secret-home-unavailable` failures'' in `kahua-joined-mount`; other founding failures also reported that error. The runner output did not preserve enough detail to count every failure by cause reliably.

->↺ The focused tests exercise the catalog and VM wrapper directly; they do ''not'' verify a complete browser boot with a proved face. The initial red-first attempt also stopped at the stale-build guard before executing tests. Those gaps and the full-suite failures leave the requested validation incomplete.

&lt;&lt;~ oracle throw=`↯12 ✲ ⚂(3) ⁂:ᚠ⊗㐂`>>
